## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design runtime-extensible plug-in architecture with thread-safe swapping and minimal churn. It emphasizes real-world needs: evolving routing logic without redeploys.

## Key Concepts

- Strategy + Registry for plugins
- Atomic or lock-free policy swap
- Metadata-driven policy selection
- Backward-compatible evolution

## Code Example

```java
interface RoutingPolicy {
  Destination route(Event e);
}

class EventRouter {
  private final Registry<RoutingPolicyFactory> registry;
  private final AtomicReference<RoutingPolicy> current;
  Destination route(Event e){ return current.get().route(e); }
}
```

